{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775248686,"nonce":"wMDJKleopaKfQOCN9+w4DQiHXh0=","title":"Print total session cost when running `nightshift accept`.","message":"`nightshift accept` merges and cleans up but doesn't show how much the session cost. The usage data is in state.json (from REQ-032) and usage.jsonl, but the user never sees it during the accept flow.\n\n\nAfter a successful merge in `cmd_accept`, read the session's usage data from state.json and print a summary line:\n\n```\nAccepted and cleaned up abc123\nCost: 45K input / 12K output tokens, $0.38 (claude-sonnet-4-6, 3 resumes)\n```\n\nIf no usage data is available (e.g. agent didn't report it), skip the line silently.\n\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_accept_prints_cost_summary\n  Assert: cmd_accept output includes \"Cost:\" line when usage data exists in state.json\n- tests/test_cli_commands.py::test_accept_no_cost_when_no_usage\n  Assert: cmd_accept output does not include \"Cost:\" when no usage data in state.json\n\n- host/cli.py (modify — add cost summary print in cmd_accept after merge)\n- core/post_run.py (use existing format_cost_line() helper)\n\n1. In host/cli.py cmd_accept, after successful merge and before cleanup:\n   - Read state.json from the session dir\n   - If state has usage data, call format_cost_line() and print it\n2. Use existing format_cost_line() from core/post_run.py (already formats usage data)\n\nSee core/post_run.py format_cost_line() for formatting.\nSee host/cli.py cmd_accept for the accept flow.\n\nREQ: REQ-032","files":null}]}